From  \[ \frac{M_d}{C_d}=1, \qquad C_d\neq 0, \]  multiplying both sides by \(C_d\) gives  \[ M_d=C_d. \]  Therefore, the following statements are equivalent:  \[ \boxed{\frac{M_d}{C_d}=1} \iff \boxed{M_d=C_d} \iff \boxed{M_d-C_d=0}, \qquad C_d\neq0. \]  In your model, this represents the **exact boundary** where mass/load equals capacity. One wording adjustment: “strictly equal” is mathematically fine, but **“exactly equal at depth \(d\)”** is clearer.